## Fleet standing rules (all machines)

- Files are the single source of truth for critical state; chat carries discussion and doorbells, never state.
- No installs or removals on any machine without the owner's explicit per-machine permission.
- Keys, tokens, and auth material never leave the machine they belong to, and never land in a project folder or on the shelf (Dropbox).
- GitHub is the source of truth for code; zones hold clones, never divergent hand-synced copies.
- This file is composed from canonical scoped sections (Fleet Harness Spec v0.6.10, §4.2). Edit the sections in the fleet-harness repo's instructions/ folder — never the composed file.
- Reporting the status of a set (Derek's corrections, 2026-10-27): when the owner asks for the status of a set — subscriptions, pools, lanes, sessions — report EVERY member of the set, the full table, never curated highlights.
- "No readout / not available" is never a conclusion: before reporting any measurement or capability as unavailable, research it properly — the tool's own commands, vendor endpoints, the web — and report only what the research actually ruled out.
- When a measurement contradicts verified reality, distrust the meter, not the reality: investigate until the two reconcile; never keep relaying a number known to be wrong.

## Building code: clean architecture first (Derek's standing rule, 2026-11-09)

- Always build code cleanly, modularly, and with proper architecture and separation of concerns. Never simply bolt on a feature because I asked for it. If you can't find an easy way to build it naturally, and you'd recommend a refactor to make the whole thing cleanly, stop your work ahead of time and say so.
- This applies to every coding lane and session on every machine, in every harness. A feature request never overrides it.

## Fated web/database test ban (Derek's standing rule, 2026-09-23)

- Agents must not run Fated web test suites (vitest, playwright, `npm run verify`) or database test suites (pgTAP/SQL runner) — locally or remotely (fleet machines included), against local or remote databases — unless Derek explicitly requests a named suite. This overrides the Fated repo's `npm run verify` pre-push gate for web/db; iOS/Android suite rules are unchanged.

